Full license text:
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode

Summary of obligations:

  Attribution (BY):
    You must credit David Nash / AstroNexus and the HYG Database v4.1
    as the source of the star data. A link to the HYG Database
    repository is recommended.

  ShareAlike (SA):
    If you redistribute or modify the derived star arrays, the result
    must be shared under CC BY-SA 4.0 (or a compatible later version).

  Indicate modifications:
    You must state that the original catalog was filtered to the 500
    brightest stars and that Right Ascension / Declination were
    converted to 3D direction vectors.

Scope of this obligation:

  This license applies ONLY to the HYG-derived star data. The rest of
  yDream Shaders (shader source files, textures, pack metadata, and
  every other asset) is distributed under the GNU Lesser General
  Public License v3.0, as stated at the top of this document.

  Where the two licenses interact — for example, a GLSL file that
  contains both shader code and the derived star arrays — the
  derived data remains under CC BY-SA 4.0 and the surrounding code
  remains under LGPL v3.0.